---
import SeoArticle from "../../components/SeoArticle.astro";
import { faq } from "./faq";
---

<SeoArticle idPrefix="ws-seo" {faq}>
  <section aria-labelledby="ws-seo-how">
    <h2 id="ws-seo-how" class="sd-text-title">How to run a writing sprint</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>
        Choose a length: 10, 15 or 25 minutes, or your own, up to three hours.
      </li>
      <li>
        Press Start sprint and write. The timer counts down and the word count
        rises as you type.
      </li>
      <li>
        When time is up, you can see how many words you wrote and how long
        the sprint ran.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      Tip: You can pause and resume the timer if you're interrupted or need to
      take a break. Also, if the timer is distracting or makes you tense, you
      can hide it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="ws-seo-tips">
    <h2 id="ws-seo-tips" class="sd-text-title">Tips for a good sprint</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Decide what you will write before you press Start, even if it's as
        simple as, "the next scene."
      </li>
      <li>
        Do not go back to fix things. Leave a note to yourself, such as [name?],
        and keep moving. Those details and edits can come later.
      </li>
      <li>
        Use the same length for a week and watch your word count. Keep track of
        your word count if you want to see your progress.
      </li>
      <li>
        Treat the draft as a first draft. The second draft is where you cut and
        reshape.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="ws-seo-privacy">
    <h2 id="ws-seo-privacy" class="sd-text-title">Your draft is yours</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing you write in this sprint leaves your computer. The draft is saved
      in your browser so it is waiting when you come back. There is no account
      and no limit on how many sprints you run.
    </p>
  </section>
</SeoArticle>
